\section{Discussion}
\label{sec:discussion}

\paragraph{Disambiguation neglect and prompt-level safety.}
The 4.6\% ambiguity awareness rate implies prompt-level safety instructions are insufficient: agents cannot flag ambiguity they do not recognize. Authorization scope responds to explicit disambiguation instructions ($-$18.0\,pp), but incompleteness does not ($-$3.4\,pp, n.s.), because missing information cannot be recovered from the prompt alone (Appendix~\ref{app:mitigation}).

